# Response headers for bindersnap.com, read by Cloudflare's static assets
# (wrangler.jsonc). GitHub Pages could send none of these, which is why
# index.html carries its own frame-busting script (#132); it stays as a second
# line of defence. Caddy sends the same set for api.bindersnap.com.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy script-src yet: the landing page and the Google
# tag on the marketing pages use inline scripts, so a script policy needs
# hashes first. frame-ancestors, object-src and base-uri cost nothing.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
